ualité ou son degré.","contrastFr":"み n’est pas librement productif avec tous les adjectifs; il faut apprendre ses mots attestés.","examples":[{"ja":"この部屋の広さに驚きました。","reading":"このへやのひろさにおどろきました。","fr":"La taille de cette pièce m’a surpris.","origin":"Original example, independent native review pending"},{"ja":"静かさが好きです。","reading":"しずかさがすきです。","fr":"J’aime le calme.","origin":"Original example, independent native review pending"},{"ja":"日本語の面白さが分かってきました。","reading":"にほんごのおもしろさがわかってきました。","fr":"Je commence à comprendre ce qui fait l’intérêt du japonais.","origin":"Original example, independent native review pending"}],"prerequisites":["grammar-verb-groups","grammar-copula","grammar-i-adjectives"],"sources":[{"url":"https://imabi.org/adjective-nominalization/","title":"Adjective Nominalization I: ～さ & ～み","publisher":"Seth Coonrod, original IMABI curriculum author","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","availability":"fetched","verification":"Source fetched; pedagogical source alignment reviewed editorially; no native review claimed","license":"Copyright retained by author; no open license verified","reuse":"Original paraphrase and examples; source lessons, recordings and illustrations not reproduced"}],"status":"editorial-draft","reviewScope":"Editorial linguistic review only; native-speaker review and learner testing pending","createdAt":"12 October 2026","learnerState":"not-assessed","oralPromptsFr":["La taille de cette pièce m’a surpris.","J’aime le calme.","Je commence à comprendre ce qui fait l’intérêt du japonais."],"levelEstimated":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageAdvancedRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":251,"revisionDate":"13 October 2026","markdown":"## adv-adjective-sa : さ : faire d’une qualité un nom (13 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N3 ; statut : editorial-draft. (13 October 2026)\n\nEnlever い d’un adjectif en い, ou な d’un adjectif en な, puis ajouter さ. いい utilise la base よい et d