 files have separate rights. ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (12 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"da5c36bf96b1bca1b20435b0f8173e312623f2283b7cfb9315a515316b71e302","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"da5c36bf96b1bca1b20435b0f8173e312623f2283b7cfb9315a515316b71e302","reviewerIds":["/root/japan_adversarial","/root/japan_review_b"],"evidenceUrls":["https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/663/"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAt":"13 October 2026","reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"japan-adv-yakushima","title":"Pourquoi Yakushima ne se réduit-il pas à quelques vieux arbres ?","domain":"geography","level":"culture","aliases":["Yakushima","屋久島","sugi","forêt"],"explanationFr":"L’intérieur de l’île de Yaku abrite des forêts tempérées chaudes, une flore riche et de très anciens sugi. L’UNESCO souligne sa position au contact de régions biogéographiques différentes. Les arbres remarquables font partie d’un système écologique et d’un gradient de milieux, plutôt que d’un simple ensemble de curiosités isolées.","scopeNote":"Cette fiche décrit le bien naturel inscrit; elle ne donne pas d’instruction de randonnée ou d’accès.","prerequisites":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/662/","title":"Yakushima","publisher":"UNESCO World Heritage Centre","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","availability":"consulted","license":"Property descriptions display CC-BY-SA IGO 3.0. Photographs, maps and nomination files have separate rights.","reuse":"Original factual synthesis and attribution; no copied description, image, map or audio."}],"backlogRefs":["japan-backlog-geography-03","japan-backlog-seasons-01"],"status":"source-reviewed-draft","claimType":"fact","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","reviewState":{"sourceClaim":"checked","japaneseExample":"not-applicable","nativeReview":"pending"},"examples":[],"levelEstimated":false,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/